<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.1: Admin Create New Campaign Setup (Step-1)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to enter the campaign name and select the campaign t=
ype so that I can initiate the phishing simulation campaign creation proces=
s with a unique setup.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>The Admin begins the campaign creation process by entering a unique camp=
aign name and selecting the campaign type. This step is critical as it sets=
 up the foundation for the entire campaign and guides the Admin through the=
 subsequent steps of the campaign creation process. The Admin's selection o=
f the campaign type determines the inclusion or exclusion of training modul=
es in the following steps.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Enters the campaign name, selects the campaign t=
ype, and progresses through the campaign setup.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the campaign setup interface, validate=
s inputs, and guides the Admin to the next step based on the selected campa=
ign type.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged in with the necessary privileges to create phishing camp=
aigns.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and supports campaign creation with a step-by-=
step setup process.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has access to the <strong>Create New Campaign</strong> interfa=
ce.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The campaign name and type are saved as the initial step of the campaign=
 setup.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin proceeds to the next step (Email Template selection) in the ca=
mpaign creation process.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p>Step-by-step wizard: 1 Campaign Setup -&gt; 2 Email Template -&gt; 3 Lan=
ding Page -&gt; 4 Mail Server -&gt; 5 Tags -&gt; 6 Audience -&gt; 7 Trainin=
g -&gt; 8 Schedule -&gt; 9 Review</p>
<p><strong>Wizard: Step 1 Campaign Setup</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Access Campaign Setup</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Campaign Management</strong> section =
and clicks on the <strong>Create New Campaign</strong> button.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Campaign Setup</strong> interface with t=
wo fields:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Name</strong>: A input field to enter a unique campaign=
 name. placeholder: Enter unique campaign name (max 50 characters)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Type</strong>: A radio button to select one of the foll=
owing campaign types:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Simulated Phishing</strong>: A phishing-only campaign without th=
e security awareness training step. p tag: Send simulated phishing emails t=
o test employee awareness and identify vulnerabilities.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</strong>: A=
 combined campaign that includes both phishing simulation and security awar=
eness training. p tag: Combined campaign with phishing simulation and immed=
iate security awareness training for caught users.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Enter Campaign Information</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin enters a unique <strong>Campaign Name</strong> (e.g., "Holiday=
 Offer").</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system validates the name to ensure it does not exceed 50 characters=
.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects a <strong>Campaign Type</strong> from the radio button=
:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If the <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> type is selected, then from w=
izard step 7 <strong>training module</strong> selection will be skipped in =
the next steps of the campaign setup.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the <strong>Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</str=
ong> type is selected, the system will include wizard step 7 for selecting =
<strong>training modules</strong> later in the setup process.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Continue to Next Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After entering the campaign name and selecting the campaign type, the <s=
trong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> to proceed to the =
next step (Email Template selection).</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Name Field</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Should not be empty.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Must be at least 3 characters long and a maximum of 50 characters.</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Campaign name is required and must be a=
t least 3 characters."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Type Field</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin must select a valid <strong>Campaign Type</strong> (Simulated =
Phishing or Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid campaign type."</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"61=
76efa3-c5eb-441b-93ec-857b287adecf" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin must enter a unique campaign name.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin must select a valid <strong>Campaign Type</strong> (Simulated =
Phishing or Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system will dynamically adjust the flow based on the selected <stron=
g>Campaign Type</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"0b=
f78995-5bef-46cd-884c-d3093571edf5" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enter a <strong>Campaign Name</strong> and it must be unique a=
nd within the character limit.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The name is entered successfully and does not exceed 50 characters.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a <strong>Campaign Type</strong> (Simulated Phishing or=
 Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The campaign type is correctly selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system dynamically adjusts the setup process based on the selected <=
strong>Campaign Type</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The flow adjusts by including or excluding the training module selection=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled once all requ=
ired fields are valid.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The button is enabled only after the valid inputs.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin cannot proceed without selecting a <strong>Campaign Type</strong>.=
</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is disabled until a vali=
d campaign type is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system displays a warning if the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> exce=
eds the character limit.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system displays an error message if the name exceeds 50 characters.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can continue to the next step only after a valid <strong>Campaign =
Name</strong> and <strong>Campaign Type</strong> are selected.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can click <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> after both fields a=
re filled correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system ensures that the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> is unique and=
 prevents duplicates.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system prevents duplicate names and displays a relevant message.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system logs the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> and <strong>Campaign =
Type</strong> for audit purposes.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The campaign details are logged once the Admin clicks <strong>Save &amp;=
 Continue</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view the selected <strong>Campaign Type</strong> and the <stro=
ng>Campaign Name</strong> in the next step of the setup process.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Both the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> and <strong>Campaign Type</stron=
g> appear in the subsequent step.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>If <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> is selected, the system skips the=
 <strong>Training Module Selection</strong> step.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system skips step 6 (Training Module Selection) when <strong>Simulat=
ed Phishing</strong> is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>If <strong>Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</strong>=
 is selected, the system includes the <strong>Training Module Selection</st=
rong> step.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system adds step 6 (Training Module Selection) when <strong>Simulate=
d Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</strong> is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> and <strong>Simulat=
ed Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</strong> without errors.</p><=
/td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The dropdown list shows both options, and Admin can select either.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is disabled until both t=
he <strong>Campaign Name</strong> and <strong>Campaign Type</strong> are fi=
lled in correctly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled only when bot=
h fields are valid.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can return to the <strong>Campaign Setup</strong> page and edit th=
e <strong>Campaign Name</strong> or <strong>Campaign Type</strong> before c=
ontinuing.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can modify the details before moving on to the next step.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system validates that the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> is within t=
he required length (3-50 characters).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>A validation error is shown if the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> is too=
 short or too long.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>If the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> is empty, the system prompts the A=
dmin to enter a name.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>An error message prompts the Admin to fill in the <strong>Campaign Name<=
/strong> field.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-18</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can change the <strong>Campaign Type</strong> after the initial se=
lection, and the flow will adjust accordingly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system dynamically adjusts the flow based on the updated selection.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-19</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can use the <strong>Search</strong> bar to find an existing campai=
gn or to track the progress of the creation process.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Search</strong> function works and allows filtering the camp=
aigns in progress.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-20</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system ensures that the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> is displayed =
as entered in the summary section after it is saved.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Campaign Name</strong> appears correctly in the summary afte=
r saving.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Name</strong>: Must be unique and within 50 characters.=
 The system validates that the name meets the minimum and maximum length re=
quirements.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Type</strong>: The system dynamically changes the setup=
 flow based on the selected campaign type:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If <strong>Simulated Phishing</strong> is selected, the training step is=
 skipped.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If <strong>Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</strong>=
 is selected, the training step is included.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Authorization</strong>: Only authorized Admins can create phishi=
ng campaigns.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Protection</strong>: All campaign data, including campaign =
names and configurations, is securely stored.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Logging</strong>: All actions related to campaign creation are l=
ogged for auditing purposes.</p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
